      "title": "GGUF Quantized Model Loader",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "🧠 TECH EXPLAINER: GGUF & QUANTIZATION\n\nWhy do we use these specific files on our budget 8GB VRAM setup?\n\n1. WHAT IS QUANTIZATION?\nAI models are originally trained in high precision (like FP32 or FP16). \nThink of it like saving a massive uncompressed 4K video file. Quantization \ncompresses the mathematical weights of the model down to smaller formats \n(like 8-bit or 6-bit). It reduces the file size and VRAM impact by up to 70%, \nallowing huge models (like Z-Image 6B) to fit into our 8GB VRAM limit!\n\n2. WHAT IS THE GGUF FORMAT?\nGGUF is a highly optimized file format designed for fast local inference. \nUnlike old formats, GGUF allows \"Split Loading\". This means ComfyUI can \nprecision-load the compressed layers directly between your System RAM \nand your VRAM without crashing.\n\n3. OUR PRODUCTION CHOICES (Q6_K):\nWe use the Q6_K format for Z-Image and Qwen3. The 'Q6' stands for 6-bit quantization. \nThis is the ultimate sweet spot for our Pascal architecture:\n-> You get 99% of the original FP16 generation quality.\n-> You save massive VRAM, completely bypassing the CUDA Out-of-Memory error.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#323",
      "bgcolor": "#535"
    },
