      "title": "Image Size",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "📐 COMPREHENSIVE RESOLUTION & ASPECT RATIO MATRIX\n\nUse these exact dimensions inside your 'Empty Latent Image' Node:\n\n1. SQUARE FORMAT (1:1)\n*   **512 x 512**   -> [1:1] Absolute Base Canvas. Optimized for Float Advanced Video Sync. Max VRAM Safety.\n*   **1024 x 1024** -> [1:1] Modern High-Res Square. (Excellent for Instagram/TikTok profile frames).\n\n2. LANDSCAPE / CINEMATIC FORMATS (WIDESCREEN)\n*   **768 x 512**   -> [3:2] Classic Cinematic Draft. Safe widescreen resolution for lower VRAM cards.\n*   **1280 x 720**  -> [16:9] Standard HD. Good balance between horizontal workspace and render speed.\n*   **1920 x 1080** -> [16:9] Full HD. The golden standard for YouTube Videos and standard VFX backgrounds.\n\n3. PORTRAIT FORMATS (VERTICAL)\n*   **512 x 768**   -> [2:3] Vertical Draft. Great for standard character test renders.\n*   **1080 x 1920** -> [9:16] Full Mobile Portrait. Perfect for YouTube Shorts, TikToks, and Instagram Reels.\n\n⚠️ PASCAL HARDWARE NOTE (Tesla P4 / 8GB VRAM):\nAlways remember that doubling the resolution quadruples the pixel count! \nFor our heavy Float Advanced audio-to-video pass, stick strictly to 512x512 \nas the core animation canvas to prevent CUDA Out-of-Memory crashes. You can \nalways upscale the final video post-render using an Ultimate SD Upscale node!\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
